    "goal": "Report the PLINK binary .bed dataset size, per-chromosome file count, and per-chromosome .bed size for a GWAS cohort of 14352 samples and 2760874 variants (918034 on the largest chromosome).",
    "rationale": "PLINK binary .bed packs 2 bits per sample per variant, so total size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome .bed uses the same rule applied to one chromosome's variant count. The number of per-chromosome files equals the number of chromosomes in the dataset; for a standard human GWAS this is 24 (22 autosomes + X + Y), or 22 if autosome-only. The largest chromosome (chr1) carries 918034 variants.",
